{"schema":"symmetry-lab-principles-provenance-1","release":"20261030-symmetry1","date":"2026-10-30","originalContent":true,"scope":"Three bounded symmetry teaching modules with explicit per-generator constraint provenance, finite symmetry-breaking predictions, passive convention checks and finite-system degeneracy diagnostics.","counts":{"modules":3,"lessons":9,"exercises":9,"cases":9,"exerciseSteps":36,"presets":24,"predictions":6,"projects":3,"projectStages":9,"retainedProjects":14,"projectCenterTotal":17,"dictionaryEntries":94,"dictionarySources":34,"catalogSources":8,"sources":42,"uniqueSourceURLs":38},"projects":[{"id":"order-to-bond-constraints","module":"order","title":"Exchange constraint from order parameter residual group to a key","stages":[{"id":"direction","title":"Determine remaining operations for 2D polarity order parameter","action":"order_parameter_lab"},{"id":"bond","title":"Specify remaining mirrors separately for keys along x","action":"exchange_symmetry_lab"},{"id":"convention","title":"Use the same key to distinguish conventions and physical violations","action":"exchange_symmetry_lab"}]},{"id":"bond-to-conserved-spin","module":"exchange","title":"From elimination DMI to global spin rotation and conservation","stages":[{"id":"dmi","title":"reserves an allowed DMI component","action":"exchange_symmetry_lab"},{"id":"inversion","title":"Only add inversion and check the symmetry part","action":"exchange_symmetry_lab"},{"id":"generators","title":"Check conservation on the same energy scale generator","action":"conservation_lab"}]},{"id":"generator-to-dephasing","module":"conservation","title":"Conserved generators and decoherence: two diagnostics for the same single spin","stages":[{"id":"unitary","title":"First distinguish conserved quantities from precessing transverse components","action":"conservation_lab"},{"id":"bath","title":"Enable only pure z  decoherence ","action":"conservation_lab"},{"id":"density","title":"Reproduce exactly the same trajectory in the density-matrix classroom","action":"density_matrix_lab"}]}],"models":[{"module":"order_parameter_lab","coverage":["Exact signed-permutation finite groups C4v (xy polar vector) and Oh (xyz polar vector); Reynolds generation of invariant polynomial bases through degree six","Stabilizers, parent orbits, field-induced orbit splitting, radial stationary points, per-generator coefficient constraints and passive-coordinate covariance"],"limitations":["Only the two declared polar-vector representations, not arbitrary space-group irreducible representations, crystal structure reconstruction or material fitting","Specified order direction need not be an equilibrium; radial stationary points are not full-space extrema; boundedness diagnostic is sufficient, not necessary"]},{"module":"exchange_symmetry_lab","coverage":["Real 3-by-3 oriented-bond exchange tensors projected onto selected finite axial-spin point-operation constraints, including bond endpoint swaps","Isotropic, antisymmetric DMI and symmetric traceless components; two-spin-half exact spectra, classical unit-spin minima, generator provenance and passive/bond convention checks"],"limitations":["A single bond with supplied synthetic meV coefficients; no full crystal exchange network, material fit, lattice magnon spectrum or thermodynamic magnetic phase","DMI sign refers to the displayed i-to-j bond and cross-product convention; swapping endpoints transposes the exchange tensor"]},{"module":"conservation_lab","coverage":["One/two spin-half Hamiltonians and independent local Lindblad channels; termwise commutators, adjoint-generator conservation diagnostics and density-matrix trajectories","Finite-system spin rotations, antiunitary covariance, Kramers square diagnostics, global-SU2 checks and invariant expectations under passive basis changes"],"limitations":["Finite Hilbert spaces with H/hbar in rad/ns and rates in inverse ns; no thermodynamic spontaneous-symmetry-breaking or Goldstone proof","Commutation with the Hamiltonian alone does not imply open-system conservation; a level coincidence or commuting observable alone does not prove robust degeneracy protection"]}],"interactionScope":{"constraints":"Finite polar-vector monomial coefficient relations, axial-spin bond equations and termwise Hamiltonian/Lindblad adjoint contributions expose which generator or term produces each displayed constraint.","predictions":"Six fixed-preset choices require a recorded prediction before calculation; answers are supported by computed model evidence, not automated grading of free-text scientific reasoning.","conventions":"Passive coordinates transform vectors, operations, exchange tensors, Hamiltonians, states, observables and antiunitary unitary parts consistently; coordinate relabeling is not physical symmetry breaking.","degeneracy":"Finite spin-half diagnostics distinguish Kramers antiunitary square, global SU2 multiplets and accidental coincidences; no complete magnetic-space-group, momentum-space or thermodynamic classification.","comparisons":"Same-calculator A/B records retain inputs and raw results; curve overlays additionally require compatible release, model, experiment and axis labels.","formulaLinks":"Twelve contextual entries preserve the original 82 entries and 30 source records. The original extensionRelease remains unchanged and principlesRelease identifies this addition.","projects":"Three new three-stage evidence projects preserve fourteen prior projects. Saved completion and prose do not assert automatic scientific grading."},"sources":[{"id":"order-isodistort","title":"ISODISTORT: distortion modes, order-parameter directions and stabilizer subgroups","url":"https://iso.byu.edu/isodistorthelp.php"},{"id":"order-isotropy","title":"ISOTROPY user manual: invariants and order parameters","url":"https://iso.byu.edu/isotropy_doc.php"},{"id":"exchange-moriya","title":"T. Moriya, Anisotropic Superexchange Interaction and Weak Ferromagnetism, Phys. Rev. 120, 91 (1960)","url":"https://journals.aps.org/pr/abstract/10.1103/PhysRev.120.91"},{"id":"exchange-feynman-angular","title":"Feynman Lectures III, Chapter 18: Angular Momentum and axial-vector transformations","url":"https://www.feynmanlectures.caltech.edu/III_18.html"},{"id":"conservation-tong","title":"David Tong: Continuous symmetry, Noether's theorem and conserved flow","url":"https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/qft/qfthtml/S1.html"},{"id":"conservation-lindblad","title":"G. Lindblad, On the generators of quantum dynamical semigroups (1976)","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01608499"},{"id":"conservation-qutip","title":"QuTiP: Operator Convention for Closed Systems and Lindblad Dynamics","url":"https://qutip.readthedocs.io/en/stable/guide/dynamics/dynamics-master.html"},{"id":"conservation-kramers","title":"MIT Quantum Theory: time reversal and Kramers theorem","url":"https://web.mit.edu/8.861/www/lect_notes/Lecture15-1.pdf"},{"id":"dictionary-iucr-hm","title":"IUCr：Hermann–Mauguin symbols","url":"https://dictionary.iucr.org/Hermann-Mauguin_symbols"},{"id":"dictionary-bilbao","title":"Bilbao Crystallographic Server: Representation and site symmetry tools","url":"https://www.cryst.ehu.es/"},{"id":"dictionary-cano","title":"Cano et al.: Elementary Band Representations (2018)","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1709.01935"},{"id":"dictionary-elcoro","title":"Elcoro et al.: Double crystallographic groups (2017)","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1706.09272"},{"id":"dictionary-phonopy","title":"Phonopy Official: dynamical matrix and thermodynamic formulas","url":"https://phonopy.github.io/phonopy/formulation.html"},{"id":"dictionary-phonopy-dsf","title":"Phonopy Official: Dynamic structure factor","url":"https://phonopy.github.io/phonopy/dynamic-structure-factor.html"},{"id":"dictionary-phonopy-qha","title":"Phonopy Official: Quasi harmonic approximation","url":"https://phonopy.github.io/phonopy/qha.html"},{"id":"dictionary-nist","title":"NIST DLMF：3j、6j、9j symbols","url":"https://dlmf.nist.gov/34"},{"id":"dictionary-pdg","title":"PDG：SU(3) isoscalar factors and representation matrices","url":"https://pdg.lbl.gov/2024/reviews/rpp2024-rev-su3-isoscalar-factors.pdf"},{"id":"dictionary-berry","title":"Xiao、Chang、Niu：Berry phase effects (2010)","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/0907.2021"},{"id":"dictionary-wannier","title":"Wannier90 official: interpolation and matrix elements","url":"https://wannier90.readthedocs.io/en/latest/user_guide/wannier90/methodology/"},{"id":"dictionary-kwant","title":"Kwant official: Quantum transport and conductance","url":"https://kwant-project.org/doc/latest/tutorial/first_steps"},{"id":"dictionary-kwant-sc","title":"Kwant Official: Superconductivity, conserved quantities and symmetry","url":"https://kwant-project.org/doc/latest/tutorial/superconductors"},{"id":"dictionary-spinw","title":"SpinW Official: Spin Waves and Correlation Functions","url":"https://spinw.org/spinwdoc/spinw_spinwave"},{"id":"dictionary-hubbard","title":"Hubbard：Electron correlations in narrow energy bands (1963)","url":"https://doi.org/10.1098/rspa.1963.0204"},{"id":"dictionary-kanamori","title":"Georges, de’ Medici, Mravlje: Hund coupling and multi-orbital correlation","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1207.3033"},{"id":"dictionary-wall","title":"Marton et al.: GLD domain wall model of BaTiO₃","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/1001.1376"},{"id":"dictionary-quanty","title":"Quanty official: NiO crystal field and many-electron state","url":"https://www.quanty.org/documentation/tutorials/nio_crystal_field/groundstate"},{"id":"dictionary-optics","title":"Armstrong et al.: Interactions between Light Waves in a Nonlinear Dielectric (1962)","url":"https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRev.127.1918"},{"id":"dictionary-magres","title":"EasySpin Official: Spin Hamiltonian","url":"https://easyspin.org/easyspin/documentation/hamiltonian.html"},{"id":"dictionary-unfold","title":"Popescu、Zunger： band unfolding (2012)","url":"https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevB.85.085201"},{"id":"dictio